From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:34:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] feat(linux): browser extensions on WebKitGTK

The port's own extension runtime, on the channel of the previous two
patches: upstream's extension install, registry and UI on Linux, the API
layer every extension context loads first (zephium-webext-linux), and the
engine's host (host/webext_linux): packages served under
chrome-extension://, one hidden background view per extension, the APIs
over the channel, toolbar actions, scripting.executeScript, insertCSS
and activeTab. Firefox add-ons install from .xpi files, their IDs derived
from the Gecko ID.

ZEPHIUM_WEBEXT_TRACE=1 logs each step of the runtime, and the background
pages' consoles. Extension files keep their Content-Type under nosniff.
